Humanoid is a MuJoCo environment with a 3D bipedal humanoid robot. The goal is to walk forward as fast as possible without falling over. This is a high-dimensional control task.
The state is a vector of 348 elements. The first 45 are the kinematic state (positions 0–21 and velocities 22–44); the remainder encode body inertia tensors, centre-of-mass velocities, actuator forces, and contact forces.
Kinematic state layout:
- state[0]: z-position of torso (height, m) — healthy range 1.0–2.0 m
- state[1–4]: quaternion orientation of torso (w, x, y, z)
- state[5]: abdomen z-angle (rad)  state[6]: abdomen y-angle  state[7]: abdomen x-angle
- state[8–10]: right hip angles (x, z, y)  state[11]: right knee angle
- state[12–14]: left hip angles (x, z, y)  state[15]: left knee angle
- state[16–17]: right shoulder angles  state[18]: right elbow angle
- state[19–20]: left shoulder angles  state[21]: left elbow angle
- state[22]: x-velocity of torso (forward speed, m/s) — maximize this
- state[23]: y-velocity of torso (lateral drift, m/s) — keep near 0
- state[24]: z-velocity of torso (m/s)
- state[25–27]: angular velocity of torso (x, y, z, rad/s)
- state[28–30]: abdomen angular velocities (z, y, x)
- state[31–34]: right hip/knee angular velocities
- state[35–38]: left hip/knee angular velocities
- state[39–41]: right shoulder/elbow angular velocities
- state[42–44]: left shoulder/elbow angular velocities
The action space is a vector of 17 float numbers representing torques applied to joints (range: -0.4 to 0.4 N):
- action[0]: abdomen_z  action[1]: abdomen_y  action[2]: abdomen_x
- action[3]: right_hip_x  action[4]: right_hip_z  action[5]: right_hip_y  action[6]: right_knee
- action[7]: left_hip_x  action[8]: left_hip_z  action[9]: left_hip_y  action[10]: left_knee
- action[11]: right_shoulder1  action[12]: right_shoulder2  action[13]: right_elbow
- action[14]: left_shoulder1  action[15]: left_shoulder2  action[16]: left_elbow
The policy is a linear policy with 5933 parameters and works as follows:
action = state @ W + b, where
state = [state[0], ..., state[347]]
W is a 348×17 matrix laid out row-major: params[i*17 .. i*17+16] = W[i,:] for i = 0..347
b = [params[5916], ..., params[5932]]
The reward function:
reward = healthy_reward + forward_reward - ctrl_cost
where:
- healthy_reward = 5.0 per step when humanoid is upright (torso height 1.0–2.0 m)
- forward_reward = 1.25 * x-velocity
- ctrl_cost = 0.1 * sum(action^2)
Episode ends early if the humanoid falls. Good policies achieve rewards of 3000–8000+.
Note: With 5933 parameters, this is a very high-dimensional optimization problem.
